# proves AtomVec::pack_comm_vel / pack_border_vel tested mask[i], the position in
# the send list, instead of mask[j], the atom, when deciding whether to apply the
# fix deform velocity remap to a ghost.
#
# Three things all have to be true for this to show:
#   - comm_modify vel yes, so ghost velocities are communicated at all
#   - a pair style that actually READS ghost velocities (granular does; lj/cut
#     does not, so the wrong values are packed but never consumed)
#   - a deform group that is not "all" -- with group all every mask matches
# The style is deterministic, so the numbers below are directly comparable.
units           lj
atom_style      sphere
dimension       3
lattice         fcc 0.6
region          box block 0 6 0 6 0 6
create_box      2 box
create_atoms    1 box
region          half block 0 3 INF INF INF INF
set             region half type 2
set             type * diameter 1.0 density 1.0
group           moving type 2
velocity        all create 1.0 87287 loop geom
pair_style      granular
pair_coeff      * * hertz/material 1e4 0.2 0.3 tangential mindlin NULL 1.0 0.5
neighbor        0.3 bin
neigh_modify    delay 0 every 1 check no
comm_modify     vel yes
fix             1 all nve/sphere
fix             2 moving deform 1 x scale 1.05 remap v units box
compute         tm moving temp/sphere
thermo_style    custom step temp c_tm epair press
thermo          25
run             50
